atural gas (RNG) plants, transportation fleet enhancements, and ecological restoration, and other projects. The company was formerly known as Hannon Armstrong Sustainable Infrastructure Capital, Inc. and changed its name to HA Sustainable Infrastructure Capital, Inc. in June 2024. HA Sustainable Infrastructure Capital, Inc. was founded in 1981 and is headquartered in Annapolis, Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeffrey A. Lipson | President, CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $3.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 173 people. Revenue per employee of $2.3M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 48%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $173K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["HA Sustainable Infrastructure C is a mid-cap financial services business with a $5.0B market cap on $401M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +19% over the past three years and +21% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 11% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 0.5% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 5.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 114% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and 